{"id": "contracting-out-city-could-staff", "title": "Contracting out: $1.79 billion where the forms say City staff have the skills", "seconds": 135.4, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "f0659c91d65c504d", "words": 413, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[0]", "timeline[1]"], "text": "4.45 billion dollars.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 2.15, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$4.45 billion", "label": "personal-services contracts Human Resources processed, fiscal 2023-24", "sub": "ceilings, not spending"}, "emph": ["4.45 billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.51, 0.67, 0.94, 1.4]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "That’s how much contracting out Human Resources counted in one year: fiscal 2023-24.", "t0": 2.67, "t1": 7.92, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Contracting out", "kicker": "Human Resources’ running total", "sub": "to 3 June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.36, 0.56, 1.1, 1.3, 1.57, 2.03, 2.36, 2.5, 2.71, 3.36, 3.62, 3.89, 4.39, 4.54]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Work given to outside firms instead of City staff.", "t0": 8.04, "t1": 10.57, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Contracting out", "kicker": "Human Resources’ running total", "sub": "to 3 June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.44, 0.58, 0.99, 1.3, 1.56, 1.65, 1.93]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 10.69, "t1": 12.2, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.25, 0.35, 0.79, 0.92, 1.0]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "form", "ref": ["story[0]", "actors[2]"], "text": "To contract out, departments must ask the Commission first. Its form asks: does the City have the skills?", "t0": 12.32, "t1": 18.28, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "The request form", "sub": "Civil Service Commission", "rows": [["Does City have classifications with the required specialized skills?", "?", 1]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.65, 1.1, 1.52, 1.78, 1.95, 2.04, 2.46, 3.07, 3.53, 3.87, 4.31, 4.75, 4.85, 5.09, 5.23, 5.4]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "The first lead. How often do departments answer yes?", "t0": 18.5, "t1": 21.93, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "164 of 242", "label": "newer forms answering yes", "sub": "181 requests, $1.79 billion, of 865 forms read"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.51, 1.08, 1.67, 1.94, 2.07, 2.53, 2.86]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "On the newer form, 164 times in 242.", "t0": 21.93, "t1": 25.99, "shot": "b4x", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "164 of 242", "label": "newer forms answering yes", "sub": "181 requests, $1.79 billion, of 865 forms read"}, "emph": ["164"], "wt": [0.04, 0.28, 0.37, 0.68, 1.06, 1.3, 1.6, 2.21, 2.64, 2.78, 2.95, 3.19]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "Those 181 forms carry 1.79 billion dollars of ceilings,", "t0": 26.11, "t1": 30.63, "shot": "b4d", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["181 forms saying City staff have the skills", "$1.79 billion"], "b": ["Human Resources’ count, fiscal 2023-24", "$4.45 billion"], "kicker": "Different sets of requests"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.43, 0.7, 1.14, 1.59, 1.92, 2.13, 2.49, 2.65, 2.93, 3.38, 3.76, 3.84]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "a different set from the 4.45 billion.", "t0": 30.63, "t1": 33.17, "shot": "b4d", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["181 forms saying City staff have the skills", "$1.79 billion"], "b": ["Human Resources’ count, fiscal 2023-24", "$4.45 billion"], "kicker": "Different sets of requests"}, "emph": ["a different set"], "wt": [0.04, 0.11, 0.47, 0.7, 0.82, 0.93, 1.18, 1.47, 1.77, 1.93]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The largest: 162.6 million dollars, for behavioral health services in locked facilities.", "t0": 33.29, "t1": 39.34, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Largest requests answering yes, millions of dollars", "rows": [["Public Health, behavioral health in locked facilities", "162.6"], ["Public Health, peer programs", "86.2"], ["Public Utilities Commission, environmental services", "75.0"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.72, 1.16, 1.51, 2.12, 2.5, 2.7, 3.04, 3.64, 3.83, 4.28, 4.5, 4.9, 5.03, 5.3]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "So why go outside? The next answer, most often: too few staff.", "t0": 39.46, "t1": 44.2, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "most often too few staff"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.24, 0.39, 1.03, 1.57, 1.78, 2.37, 2.59, 3.22, 3.53, 3.8]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "suspicious[0].what", "innocent[4]"], "text": "In the largest, the reason given is buildings: the City doesn’t own enough properties.", "t0": 44.32, "t1": 48.51, "shot": "b6b", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "does not own enough properties to operate additional specialized programs"}, "emph": ["buildings"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.17, 0.74, 0.83, 1.16, 1.48, 1.7, 2.49, 2.64, 2.89, 3.22, 3.35, 3.57]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "Its earlier ceiling, 224,217,000 dollars,", "t0": 48.63, "t1": 52.27, "shot": "b6c", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Earlier ceiling, request DHRPSC0001757", "$224,217,000"], "b": ["Crestwood Behavioral Health agreement", "$224,216,994"], "kicker": "now $386,827,830 to 1 July 2031"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.52, 1.12, 1.43, 1.56, 1.78, 2.27, 2.62, 2.71, 3.04]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "is within 6 dollars of the Crestwood locked-beds agreement.", "t0": 52.27, "t1": 55.28, "shot": "b6c", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Earlier ceiling, request DHRPSC0001757", "$224,217,000"], "b": ["Crestwood Behavioral Health agreement", "$224,216,994"], "kicker": "now $386,827,830 to 1 July 2031"}, "emph": ["within 6 dollars"], "wt": [0.04, 0.13, 0.48, 0.73, 1.06, 1.17, 1.28, 1.8, 2.39]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The second lead. Of 301 newer forms, 241 call the need long-term, not temporary.", "t0": 55.5, "t1": 62.01, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Call the need long-term", "241 of 301"], "b": ["No plan to bring the work back", "209 of 241"]}, "emph": ["long-term"], "wt": [0.0, 0.02, 0.36, 0.86, 1.35, 1.61, 1.89, 2.09, 2.4, 3.12, 3.21, 3.49, 4.04, 4.32, 4.43, 4.69, 5.62, 5.82]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "And 209 of 241 say there’s no plan to bring the work back to City staff.", "t0": 62.13, "t1": 66.65, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Call the need long-term", "241 of 301"], "b": ["No plan to bring the work back", "209 of 241"]}, "emph": ["no plan"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.21, 0.45, 0.77, 0.89, 1.0, 1.17, 1.72, 2.14, 2.37, 2.52, 2.81, 2.89, 3.07, 3.17, 3.43, 3.61, 3.69, 3.93]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "That’s a standing decision to keep the work outside the civil service.", "t0": 66.77, "t1": 70.05, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a standing decision to keep the work outside the civil service"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.26, 0.66, 1.1, 1.17, 1.31, 1.47, 1.76, 2.36, 2.46, 2.72]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead. 93 amendments enlarged approvals first given six or more years earlier.", "t0": 70.27, "t1": 75.47, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "93", "label": "amendments enlarging approvals six or more years old"}, "emph": ["93"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.47, 1.3, 1.72, 2.24, 2.65, 3.13, 3.52, 3.85, 4.02, 4.11, 4.31, 4.58]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "One old Airport approval now reaches 1.60 billion dollars.", "t0": 75.59, "t1": 79.37, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.60 billion", "label": "Airport Commission 40697-14/15, as amended"}, "emph": ["1.60 billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.45, 0.84, 1.27, 1.52, 1.9, 2.04, 2.33, 2.6, 2.92, 3.32]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "innocent[2]"], "text": "An amendment raises an old ceiling. The case for contracting out isn’t made again.", "t0": 79.79, "t1": 84.29, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the case for contracting out is not made again from the start"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.56, 0.89, 1.01, 1.16, 1.79, 2.48, 2.68, 2.82, 3.31, 3.58, 3.88, 4.09]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "The fourth lead. 25 new requests gave start dates more than 30 days before their hearing.", "t0": 84.51, "t1": 89.48, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "25", "label": "new requests started more than 30 days before their hearing"}, "emph": ["25"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.39, 1.05, 1.67, 1.83, 2.35, 2.55, 2.82, 3.07, 3.2, 3.35, 3.69, 3.95, 4.26, 4.41]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "One, a 7.5 million dollar Technology request, started in November 2015.", "t0": 89.6, "t1": 94.4, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Technology 44123-22/23, $7.5 million, started", "1 November 2015"], "b": ["Heard by the Commission", "7 November 2022"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.63, 0.71, 0.99, 1.29, 1.45, 1.83, 2.05, 2.58, 3.11, 3.42, 3.5, 3.84, 4.13]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "It was heard in November 2022.", "t0": 94.52, "t1": 96.36, "shot": "b13x", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Technology 44123-22/23, $7.5 million, started", "1 November 2015"], "b": ["Heard by the Commission", "7 November 2022"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.03, 0.16, 0.31, 0.44, 0.85, 1.16]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "The Commission was asked after the fact.", "t0": 96.48, "t1": 98.39, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Technology 44123-22/23, $7.5 million, started", "1 November 2015"], "b": ["Heard by the Commission", "7 November 2022"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.49, 0.69, 1.03, 1.32, 1.45]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[1]"], "text": "The fifth lead. 6 requests were contested before the Commission, worth 86.4 million dollars.", "t0": 98.61, "t1": 104.99, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "6 contested requests", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "$86.4 million, heard as separate items"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.45, 1.09, 1.89, 2.33, 2.49, 2.94, 3.14, 3.28, 3.95, 4.21, 4.78, 5.14, 5.29, 5.7]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[1]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "In one, a factfinder found no compelling reason, and no formal study of using City staff.", "t0": 105.11, "t1": 109.85, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "did no formal study of using City staff"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.67, 0.79, 1.31, 1.58, 1.7, 2.11, 2.62, 2.73, 2.91, 3.25, 3.55, 3.64, 3.91, 4.14]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[3]", "story[9]"], "text": "An approval is a ceiling over five years or more, not a year’s spending.", "t0": 110.07, "t1": 113.35, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a ceiling on what may be spent over the life of the contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.46, 0.58, 0.66, 0.99, 1.2, 1.45, 1.66, 1.8, 2.31, 2.45, 2.52, 2.79]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The packets don’t show what was spent, the vacancies in each class, or any refusal.", "t0": 113.47, "t1": 117.66, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["What was spent against each ceiling", "Vacancies in the classes each form names", "How often the Commission refuses or cuts a request"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.41, 0.62, 0.81, 0.95, 1.09, 1.73, 1.83, 2.36, 2.47, 2.65, 3.16, 3.31, 3.58]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[4]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The minutes do show cuts: in 2025, three of four Public Health requests were approved for less.", "t0": 117.78, "t1": 123.46, "shot": "b18c", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Public Health requests, June 2025 list: asked and approved, millions of dollars", "rows": [["Unarmed guards", "$30.0 asked, $18.0 approved"], ["Wraparound services", "$30.0 asked, $25.5 approved"], ["Program administration", "$16.0 asked, $8.5 approved"]]}, "emph": ["cuts"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.4, 0.58, 0.82, 1.62, 1.71, 1.96, 2.78, 3.07, 3.24, 3.45, 3.76, 3.99, 4.44, 4.64, 4.97, 5.14]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? Payments under the largest approvals, and vacancy counts for each class named.", "t0": 123.58, "t1": 128.31, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Invoices or payments under the ten largest approvals"}, {"who": "", "what": "Vacancy counts for the classes named on the forms"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.27, 0.55, 1.19, 1.66, 1.79, 1.88, 2.22, 2.8, 2.95, 3.34, 3.6, 3.74, 3.95, 4.24]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The Charter provides this route, and no authority has found any request improper.", "t0": 128.43, "t1": 132.12, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.03, 0.31, 0.69, 0.86, 1.37, 1.51, 1.64, 2.03, 2.18, 2.43, 2.59, 3.06]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 132.24, "t1": 134.46, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.3, 0.41, 0.53, 1.24, 1.39, 1.53]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "One year", "lead1": "Lead 1 · the City has the skills", "lead2": "Lead 2 · no plan to bring it back", "lead3": "Lead 3 · old approvals", "lead4": "Lead 4 · started first", "lead5": "Lead 5 · contested", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "terminal", "hook": "number"}